# ── Secrets scaffold (EXAMPLE — copy to a real secrets source, NEVER commit the real one) ──
# .gitignore excludes *.env except *.example.env. In real deployment these are populated
# from a secrets manager / mounted file, not this file. See internal/secrets/secrets.go.

# Door 3 — the global HMAC email-hash pepper. THE MOST FRAGILE SECRET IN THE SYSTEM.
# Generated ONCE with strong entropy; stored OUTSIDE the DB; redundant, geo-separate,
# access-audited backups; recovery DRILLED before P1 ships; rotation additive-only.
# Losing it de-joins ALL history forever; leaking it makes addresses brute-forceable.
# (Example value below is NOT a real pepper — generate your own, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.)
TM_PEPPER=REPLACE_WITH_32_BYTES_OF_ENTROPY_never_this_placeholder

# The service-role key gating ALL state. DDL/grant-admin is a SEPARATE break-glass cred
# (PN-9 / DR-3), not this one.
TM_SUPABASE_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY

# Caller -> control-plane bearer. Per-caller keys + rotation is a P5-bulk gate (PN-13 / §3.8).
TM_FRONTDOOR_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_FRONT_DOOR_BEARER

# control-plane -> verifier-node node tokens: "nodeid=token,nodeid2=token2". Per-node unique (P3 §6.4).
# Referenced by node id from the config node-list; never stored in the nodes table in clear.
TM_NODE_TOKENS=

# control-plane -> vendor keys (P6): "millionverifier=key". Layer stays DISABLED until a key + DPA exist.
TM_VENDOR_KEYS=

# ── Non-secret runtime knobs (safe to set in plain config; shown here for convenience) ──
# TM_ENV=production
# TM_LISTEN_ADDR=:8080
# Kill-switch ladder (operator can pull a rung by config, no redeploy — Door 5):
# TM_SMTP_MODE=disabled        # enabled|disabled  (P0/P1 default: disabled — no SMTP infra)
# TM_FALLBACK_MODE=off         # enabled|off       (P0/P1 default: off — no vendor)
# TM_FRONTDOOR_MODE=serving    # serving|accept_and_defer|reject
# A single node keeps the LIST shape exercised (Door 5):
# TM_NODE_ID=mock-1
# TM_NODE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# TM_NODE_ENABLED=false
